# Template for `strava.properties`. Copy this file to
# `strava.properties` (gitignored sibling, same directory) and fill in
# the credentials from https://www.strava.com/settings/api. See
# `docs/STRAVA.md` for the full walkthrough, including how to mint a
# refresh token with the `activity:write` scope.
#
# ALL OF THIS IS OPTIONAL. Strava upload is configured in the app under
# Settings -> Strava, and works on a build that carries nothing here.
# What these values buy you is a personal build that arrives pre-filled
# and already switched on: StravaStore.seedFromBuildConfig copies them
# into the editable settings on first run, once. Edits and "Forget
# credentials" in Settings win from then on.
#
# This file is the primary source for BuildConfig.STRAVA_CLIENT_ID,
# _CLIENT_SECRET and _REFRESH_TOKEN — it overrides the matching
# LIGPSPORT_STRAVA_* env vars when present.
#
# The secret is embedded in the APK: Strava requires client_secret for
# the token refresh and does not support PKCE, so there is nowhere else
# for it to live in a native app. Don't distribute a build that has
# real credentials baked in — anyone can extract them and act as your
# API application. Rotate on the settings page if that happens.
client_id=
client_secret=
# Per-athlete rather than per-application, so leave this empty unless
# the build is only for you. Strava rotates it on first use.
refresh_token=
